WAREHOUSE RECEIVING SYSTEM - USER GUIDE,
,
,
1. PREPARING DAILY SHEETS,Never type transaction data directly into the 'Master Report' sheet tab.
,"Right-click the 'Master Report' tab, select 'Move or Copy...', check 'Create a copy', and rename the tab with your new PO number (e.g., PO-406)."
2. COUNTING & INSPECTION,Physically unbox and count every individual unit delivered. Cross-reference actual counts against your original PO specifications.
,Note down the specific structural storage bay or shelf numbers inside the 'Location / Bin #' column for complete inventory logging.
3. RECORDING DISCREPANCIES,"If cargo units arrive fractured or broken, enter the number of damaged items directly into the 'Qty Damaged' ledger column."
,The cell background will automatically update to alert downstream corporate accounts payable verification agents.
,Set the 'Overall Shipment Status' dropdown flag in the top right to match the condition of the freight.
4. LINKING TO THE SUMMARY,Navigate to the 'Monthly Summary' sheet tab to enter a newly logged shipment.
,"Go to the first blank row. In each cell, type an equals sign (=), then click onto your new daily shipment sheet tab, select the matching cell, and press Enter."
,Example for Item Description: Type '=' in Column D -> click your new sheet tab -> select the main product cell -> press Enter.